Tunnel modifications replace the upstream server with authenticated loopback
framing, bounded owned H264 buffers, explicit stop and watchdogs. Display capture,
shell context initialization, codec lifecycle, and physical display token/power
reflection patterns are adapted. Input, semantic node rendering, consent and
session control use independent Tunnel implementations. Upstream audio, clipboard,
file transfer, settings modifications and desktop components are not included.

This is not an official scrcpy build or a claim of device compatibility.
